1
00:00:03,003 --> 00:00:06,548
♪

2
00:00:07,633 --> 00:00:08,800
[YUKINE] The only person I met

3
00:00:08,884 --> 00:00:11,094
whose existence seemed
to defy reality

4
00:00:11,178 --> 00:00:12,638
was my own sister.

5
00:00:13,555 --> 00:00:15,933
She was
a naturally brilliant mage

6
00:00:16,016 --> 00:00:18,018
and a martial arts machine
as well.

7
00:00:18,810 --> 00:00:21,939
So I lost every single
sparring match against her.

8
00:00:22,022 --> 00:00:23,982
Sure, she was two years older,

9
00:00:24,066 --> 00:00:26,818
but I only got skeptical looks
when I asked if I'd reached

10
00:00:26,902 --> 00:00:29,071
-her level by the same age.
-[gasps]

11
00:00:30,030 --> 00:00:32,032
[grunts, gasps]

12
00:00:33,742 --> 00:00:34,785
Within time,

13
00:00:35,369 --> 00:00:37,871
I was convinced I had no hope
of ever catching up to her.

14
00:00:39,581 --> 00:00:41,208
[YUKINE'S SISTER]
You're a true genius, Yukine.

15
00:00:41,833 --> 00:00:44,336
I'm positive that you are.
[chuckles]

16
00:00:45,629 --> 00:00:46,797
[YUKINE] Of course,

17
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:49,216
my inferiority
was set from the start.

18
00:00:49,967 --> 00:00:51,260
Mother and Father never tried

19
00:00:51,343 --> 00:00:53,595
to hide which child
their devotion belonged to.

20
00:00:55,013 --> 00:00:56,765
Enchanted by her swordsmanship,

21
00:00:57,182 --> 00:00:58,892
they gave her
all of their attention.

22
00:00:59,726 --> 00:01:02,521
The most painful part
was that I understood why.

23
00:01:03,355 --> 00:01:04,314
After all,

24
00:01:04,982 --> 00:01:06,275
there was no one more bewitched

25
00:01:06,358 --> 00:01:08,986
and obsessed with
my sister's talents than me.

26
00:01:09,444 --> 00:01:10,570
She was a genius.

27
00:01:12,155 --> 00:01:14,533
I could never surpass her
with a katana,

28
00:01:14,616 --> 00:01:16,827
but there was always
a chance with magic,

29
00:01:16,910 --> 00:01:18,328
so I focused on that.

30
00:01:18,412 --> 00:01:19,329
Huh?

31
00:01:20,664 --> 00:01:23,375
[YUKINE] I knew I had
some talent for swordsmanship,

32
00:01:24,126 --> 00:01:25,669
but it was my insecurity
that led me

33
00:01:25,752 --> 00:01:27,129
to choose the naginata.

34
00:01:28,672 --> 00:01:30,966
Knowing I had
some skill with the katana

35
00:01:31,049 --> 00:01:33,844
only made me more aware
of how gifted she was.

36
00:01:36,597 --> 00:01:38,307
And that decision
was the first time

37
00:01:38,390 --> 00:01:39,349
that I ran away.

38
00:01:47,441 --> 00:01:48,567
[both gasp]

39
00:01:48,650 --> 00:01:49,818
[all gasp]

40
00:01:49,901 --> 00:01:51,903
[panting]

41
00:01:54,948 --> 00:01:57,159
I'm not the genius
you think I am.

42
00:01:57,659 --> 00:02:01,246
I'm only human, the same as you.
And you know what that means?

43
00:02:02,456 --> 00:02:05,459
You're a genius too,
so just accept it.

44
00:02:07,294 --> 00:02:10,130
You still cast
a long shadow, sis.

45
00:02:12,049 --> 00:02:14,801
[♪ opening theme song playing]

46
00:03:42,639 --> 00:03:44,474
[RUIJA] So
your ability assessments will be

47
00:03:44,558 --> 00:03:45,767
conducted in this order

48
00:03:45,851 --> 00:03:47,477
over the course
of those four days.

49
00:03:47,561 --> 00:03:50,856
The total score is combined from
the written and practical tests,

50
00:03:50,939 --> 00:03:52,274
and your results in the dungeon.

51
00:03:52,357 --> 00:03:53,525
You might feel nervous

52
00:03:53,608 --> 00:03:55,527
considering this is
your first assessment,

53
00:03:55,610 --> 00:03:58,029
so I suggest you prepare
as much as possible,

54
00:03:58,113 --> 00:04:00,532
especially since
the ranking will be made public.

55
00:04:00,615 --> 00:04:01,783
-[students groan]
-[smirks]

56
00:04:01,867 --> 00:04:03,869
♪

57
00:04:03,952 --> 00:04:05,620
[KATARINA] All right, Kousuke.

58
00:04:05,704 --> 00:04:07,747
I think it's time
you tell us the truth.

59
00:04:07,831 --> 00:04:09,416
-[KOUSUKE] Huh?
-[KATARINA] Come clean.

60
00:04:09,499 --> 00:04:11,626
What are you really doing
when you skip class?

61
00:04:11,710 --> 00:04:12,878
[KOUSUKE] It's no secret.

62
00:04:12,961 --> 00:04:15,088
I'm exploring
whatever dungeons I can.

63
00:04:15,172 --> 00:04:17,215
[KATARINA] No way.
If that's all there is to it,

64
00:04:17,299 --> 00:04:18,675
explain the rumors then.

65
00:04:18,759 --> 00:04:20,677
Losers without
a life of their own?

66
00:04:20,760 --> 00:04:23,096
Only insignificant zeroes
filled with envy

67
00:04:23,180 --> 00:04:24,639
would spread such slander.

68
00:04:25,056 --> 00:04:26,475
Please don't
let the other students

69
00:04:26,558 --> 00:04:27,726
hear you say that.

70
00:04:27,809 --> 00:04:29,060
Back up. What rumors?

71
00:04:29,144 --> 00:04:31,688
First off, that you hold
devil-worship rituals

72
00:04:31,772 --> 00:04:33,064
with some weird device,

73
00:04:33,148 --> 00:04:35,984
that you're overseeing
some shady financial deal,

74
00:04:36,067 --> 00:04:37,277
and that you skip class

75
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:39,654
to apply some kind of
pink sex lotion.

76
00:04:39,738 --> 00:04:41,364
There's a lot of truth in there.

77
00:04:41,448 --> 00:04:43,533
-[KATARINA] What? They're true?!
-By the way,

78
00:04:43,617 --> 00:04:45,202
based on her spending,
it seems a certain

79
00:04:45,285 --> 00:04:46,870
pink-haired teacher
took out a loan.

80
00:04:46,953 --> 00:04:48,830
[KOUSUKE] Really, Ms. Ruija?

81
00:04:48,914 --> 00:04:50,665
Her allowance
is more than ample!

82
00:04:51,291 --> 00:04:53,627
Hey, let's all hit
the dungeon after school!

83
00:04:53,710 --> 00:04:55,670
[KATARINA]
And tarnish my reputation?

84
00:04:56,338 --> 00:04:57,339
You should join us, Iori.

85
00:04:58,215 --> 00:04:59,799
[gasps] Can I really?

86
00:04:59,883 --> 00:05:02,344
Yeah, I've been wanting
to do a dungeon crawl with you.

87
00:05:02,969 --> 00:05:04,262
-[KATARINA] Reality check.
-[BOTH] Uh?

88
00:05:04,346 --> 00:05:05,555
First years aren't allowed

89
00:05:05,639 --> 00:05:07,516
to go dungeon exploring
without permission.

90
00:05:07,599 --> 00:05:09,017
Which you're never gonna get.

91
00:05:09,100 --> 00:05:12,562
-[KOUSUKE] Oh, I got permission.
-[IORI] From Ms. Ruija?

92
00:05:12,646 --> 00:05:14,523
[KATARINA] Damn,
our homeroom teacher?

93
00:05:14,606 --> 00:05:16,525
[KOUSUKE] I promise
we'll all be safe.

94
00:05:16,608 --> 00:05:18,610
And I'm inviting someone
on the Morals Committee.

95
00:05:18,693 --> 00:05:20,111
[KATARINA] Like, you know them?

96
00:05:20,195 --> 00:05:21,571
Are you in, Ludie?

97
00:05:22,155 --> 00:05:24,533
I mean, with all the time
you spend on the treadmill.

98
00:05:24,616 --> 00:05:26,368
-[gasps, whimpers]
-[IORI] Wow, that's so cool!

99
00:05:26,451 --> 00:05:28,495
[KATARINA] You work hard
for a princess, huh?

100
00:05:28,578 --> 00:05:30,288
But how does he know
your routine?

101
00:05:30,372 --> 00:05:32,290
That's 'cause we-- [yelps]

102
00:05:32,707 --> 00:05:34,960
[KATARINA] Well,
as long as we have permission.

103
00:05:35,043 --> 00:05:37,003
[IORI] I'm definitely in!
Thanks, Kousuke!

104
00:05:37,087 --> 00:05:38,630
All right! See you then!

105
00:05:39,214 --> 00:05:42,509
[machine beeping]

106
00:05:42,592 --> 00:05:45,387
This better not be anything
like that last dungeon.

107
00:05:45,470 --> 00:05:46,846
Nothing to worry about.

108
00:05:46,930 --> 00:05:49,641
With the in-game event
that's barreling towards us,

109
00:05:49,724 --> 00:05:51,351
we all need more combat skills.

110
00:05:52,060 --> 00:05:53,478
To be properly prepared,

111
00:05:53,562 --> 00:05:55,981
I need every last one
of them to get stronger.

112
00:05:59,734 --> 00:06:01,653
-Easy prey!
-And one for me!

113
00:06:01,736 --> 00:06:03,446
[both groan]

114
00:06:03,530 --> 00:06:04,990
♪

115
00:06:05,073 --> 00:06:06,825
Those two show
some real promise.

116
00:06:06,908 --> 00:06:09,286
Oh, trust me,
they're gonna live up to it.

117
00:06:09,911 --> 00:06:11,288
Slow your roll, you two!

118
00:06:11,371 --> 00:06:12,956
Ignore the enemies
that aren't in your way!

119
00:06:13,039 --> 00:06:15,041
[KATARINA] What? But why?

120
00:06:15,125 --> 00:06:16,960
Because we're here to run!

121
00:06:21,464 --> 00:06:22,674
[roars]

122
00:06:22,757 --> 00:06:24,801
-[all panting]
-[GOBLIN] Huh?

123
00:06:27,178 --> 00:06:29,347
[groans]

124
00:06:29,431 --> 00:06:30,765
[Katarina panting]

125
00:06:30,849 --> 00:06:32,934
You know, it would've
been nice if you'd warned us

126
00:06:33,018 --> 00:06:34,227
about all the running!

127
00:06:34,311 --> 00:06:36,479
I mean, what's even
the point of all this?

128
00:06:36,563 --> 00:06:38,315
[YUKINE] Seems
you're holding up fine, Ludie!

129
00:06:38,398 --> 00:06:40,275
Someone recently taught me

130
00:06:40,358 --> 00:06:42,110
it's all about
maintaining stamina.

131
00:06:42,193 --> 00:06:44,988
[panting] You guys are so tough!

132
00:06:45,071 --> 00:06:47,407
Well, hey, you're keeping up
with us, aren't you?

133
00:06:47,490 --> 00:06:49,034
Thanks! That's a good point!

134
00:06:51,536 --> 00:06:52,495
[NANAMI] We made it in time.

135
00:06:55,123 --> 00:06:56,374
-[YUKINE] Whoa. What?
-There's still

136
00:06:56,458 --> 00:06:57,500
a whole other level?

137
00:06:57,584 --> 00:06:59,794
If we hit
the four-way intersection,

138
00:06:59,878 --> 00:07:01,921
it's north, west, west, south.

139
00:07:02,005 --> 00:07:05,425
For the T-crossing, it's south,
south, east, south, east, north.

140
00:07:05,884 --> 00:07:07,218
Duly noted!

141
00:07:07,302 --> 00:07:10,096
Hang on. How do you know?

142
00:07:10,180 --> 00:07:11,681
[scoffs, grunts]

143
00:07:12,474 --> 00:07:14,225
[monster roars]

144
00:07:14,851 --> 00:07:16,561
[yells]

145
00:07:19,606 --> 00:07:22,192
[NANAMI] Well, Master,
one hour, 58 minutes.

146
00:07:22,275 --> 00:07:24,402
Two minutes to spare.
That was a close one.

147
00:07:24,486 --> 00:07:26,321
That was real? He did that?

148
00:07:26,404 --> 00:07:28,365
-Only one hit?
-[ALL] Huh?

149
00:07:30,408 --> 00:07:31,910
[GODDESS STATUE] Well done.

150
00:07:31,993 --> 00:07:34,204
To defeat the evil
and stand here before me

151
00:07:34,287 --> 00:07:35,580
is an impressive feat.

152
00:07:35,664 --> 00:07:39,334
To reward your heroics,
I will grant you a skill.

153
00:07:41,670 --> 00:07:43,088
Okay, what just happened?

154
00:07:43,171 --> 00:07:44,798
I think we deserve
some kind of explanation!

155
00:07:44,881 --> 00:07:47,634
Yeah, are we allowed
to gain skills this easily?

156
00:07:47,717 --> 00:07:48,927
This isn't cheating,
right, Kousuke?

157
00:07:49,010 --> 00:07:51,054
We've charted
the eight possible layouts

158
00:07:51,137 --> 00:07:52,305
of the maze
we just passed through

159
00:07:52,389 --> 00:07:54,599
and collected them
into a map for you.

160
00:07:54,683 --> 00:07:56,267
It also details the five skills

161
00:07:56,351 --> 00:07:58,186
the goddess statue
will grant you.

162
00:07:58,269 --> 00:08:00,230
-Make good use of it.
-[ALL] Huh?

163
00:08:00,313 --> 00:08:02,399
That's too much. There's no way
I can accept that!

164
00:08:02,482 --> 00:08:04,192
Yeah, you can't hand out

165
00:08:04,275 --> 00:08:05,610
that kind of intel
like it's nothing!

166
00:08:05,694 --> 00:08:08,029
I'm giving you the chance
to grow as strong as me.

167
00:08:08,113 --> 00:08:10,782
-[KATARINA] You what?!
-Please take them.

168
00:08:12,867 --> 00:08:15,662
I believe he wants us
to grow stronger together,

169
00:08:15,745 --> 00:08:17,664
but he certainly has
a weird way of showing it.

170
00:08:18,707 --> 00:08:19,791
Uh, Yukine?

171
00:08:20,625 --> 00:08:23,002
[water rushing]

172
00:08:25,088 --> 00:08:26,840
[YUKINE] My sister
was the first seemingly

173
00:08:26,923 --> 00:08:28,425
impossible person I knew.

174
00:08:29,175 --> 00:08:31,052
But then I enrolled
in the academy,

175
00:08:31,720 --> 00:08:32,846
where I met not only

176
00:08:32,929 --> 00:08:34,806
"Goddess of War"
President Monica,

177
00:08:34,889 --> 00:08:37,058
but also
our wildly powerful principal.

178
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:39,436
And after that,

179
00:08:39,519 --> 00:08:41,688
I was convinced
nobody else could surprise me.

180
00:08:42,272 --> 00:08:44,482
I knew that I could catch up
to them someday,

181
00:08:44,941 --> 00:08:46,609
and that fueled my tenacity.

182
00:08:47,360 --> 00:08:48,236
But then,

183
00:08:49,279 --> 00:08:52,657
in walks Kousuke Takioto,
and he's even younger than me.

184
00:08:52,741 --> 00:08:54,409
♪

185
00:08:55,118 --> 00:08:56,578
I know he's abnormal,

186
00:08:57,328 --> 00:08:58,788
both physically and mentally,

187
00:08:58,872 --> 00:09:00,790
and especially
in his mana capacity.

188
00:09:01,999 --> 00:09:04,210
It's like he's tapped
into the Dragon Vein,

189
00:09:04,294 --> 00:09:05,545
the source of all mana.

190
00:09:06,838 --> 00:09:08,339
I'm ashamed to admit it,

191
00:09:08,423 --> 00:09:11,134
but I was relieved to learn
he can't use emission magic.

192
00:09:13,386 --> 00:09:15,430
I still vividly remember
that day.

193
00:09:16,264 --> 00:09:17,974
He asked my advice on weapons.

194
00:09:18,641 --> 00:09:21,144
So I gave him a katana
and watched him fumble.

195
00:09:21,561 --> 00:09:23,521
I know my standards
are unfairly high

196
00:09:23,605 --> 00:09:25,356
thanks to my sister's aptitude.

197
00:09:26,149 --> 00:09:28,943
And yet, still I thought,
"He has no talent."

198
00:09:30,653 --> 00:09:33,490
But only a few days later,
he left me utterly shocked.

199
00:09:34,824 --> 00:09:36,242
He suddenly swung his sword

200
00:09:36,326 --> 00:09:38,828
as though he'd been practicing
the technique for years.

201
00:09:42,290 --> 00:09:43,374
There's a chance

202
00:09:43,792 --> 00:09:45,502
he could even learn
one of the secret techniques

203
00:09:45,585 --> 00:09:46,711
of Kyohachi-ryu.

204
00:09:47,754 --> 00:09:48,880
That specific technique,

205
00:09:49,589 --> 00:09:50,840
it was so oddly complex,

206
00:09:50,924 --> 00:09:52,967
not even my sister
could master it.

207
00:09:54,594 --> 00:09:55,970
-[grunts]
-[slashes]

208
00:09:56,054 --> 00:09:57,347
[water splashing]

209
00:09:57,430 --> 00:09:58,807
[water rushing]

210
00:10:01,226 --> 00:10:02,977
[panting]

211
00:10:05,188 --> 00:10:06,689
-Um, Yukine?
-[gasps]

212
00:10:08,608 --> 00:10:10,902
[KOUSUKE] So,
did something upset you?

213
00:10:11,486 --> 00:10:13,655
[Yukine chuckles]
What makes you think that?

214
00:10:14,197 --> 00:10:17,450
[KOUSUKE] Well, I guess that
you seemed a bit less graceful

215
00:10:17,534 --> 00:10:19,327
than normal with your naginata.

216
00:10:20,578 --> 00:10:22,497
That's a fair observation.

217
00:10:22,580 --> 00:10:23,915
[KOUSUKE]
Is something on your mind?

218
00:10:24,457 --> 00:10:26,751
Well, it's someone,
not something.

219
00:10:27,460 --> 00:10:28,753
It's strange.

220
00:10:29,129 --> 00:10:31,130
This isn't the type of thing
I would normally share with you,

221
00:10:31,631 --> 00:10:33,341
but a part of me
feels compelled to.

222
00:10:34,300 --> 00:10:35,802
What's more strange,

223
00:10:35,885 --> 00:10:38,555
I feel like I'll find the answer
I'm looking for if I do.

224
00:10:39,055 --> 00:10:40,098
I've always wondered

225
00:10:40,181 --> 00:10:41,683
how strong
I can actually become.

226
00:10:42,433 --> 00:10:43,434
My touchstone

227
00:10:43,852 --> 00:10:46,229
was to surpass the one person
I could never beat.

228
00:10:47,063 --> 00:10:49,566
I'm talking about my big sister.

229
00:10:50,149 --> 00:10:51,317
It's funny, though.

230
00:10:51,609 --> 00:10:54,529
She insisted I could be
the strongest in the world.

231
00:10:54,612 --> 00:10:56,948
She wanted me to claim
that title in her place.

232
00:10:57,031 --> 00:10:58,658
And I promised her I would.

233
00:10:59,284 --> 00:11:00,827
I'm positive
you'll be in the running

234
00:11:00,910 --> 00:11:02,412
for the world's strongest.

235
00:11:02,495 --> 00:11:04,414
Won't be easy getting past me,
though.

236
00:11:04,497 --> 00:11:05,665
[laughs]

237
00:11:05,748 --> 00:11:08,835
Hang on, just let me finish.
Where was I?

238
00:11:08,918 --> 00:11:11,546
No matter how much
I've grown over all these years,

239
00:11:11,629 --> 00:11:13,715
my sister still towers over me.

240
00:11:14,591 --> 00:11:17,093
What's worse, she still does it
from beyond the grave.

241
00:11:17,177 --> 00:11:18,094
[gasps]

242
00:11:18,178 --> 00:11:19,345
♪

243
00:11:19,679 --> 00:11:20,889
[KOUSUKE] You don't get
much detailed discussion

244
00:11:20,972 --> 00:11:22,223
in the game,

245
00:11:22,307 --> 00:11:24,058
but I do know
her sister died young.

246
00:11:24,642 --> 00:11:28,062
I still kept up my training
and then enrolled at the school.

247
00:11:28,146 --> 00:11:30,857
It was shocking to meet people
as brilliant as my sister.

248
00:11:30,940 --> 00:11:32,275
[water flowing]

249
00:11:32,358 --> 00:11:33,443
I sort of understand

250
00:11:33,526 --> 00:11:35,612
that people
have expectations for me.

251
00:11:36,154 --> 00:11:38,531
Some of them, like you,
even say it to my face.

252
00:11:39,741 --> 00:11:40,700
Still...

253
00:11:41,451 --> 00:11:42,744
I can't help but question

254
00:11:42,827 --> 00:11:44,787
whether I can live up
to people's hopes for me.

255
00:11:44,871 --> 00:11:47,123
I try my hardest
to believe my sister's words

256
00:11:47,207 --> 00:11:49,083
and do everything
I can to get stronger,

257
00:11:49,167 --> 00:11:50,793
but that only does so much.

258
00:11:51,628 --> 00:11:53,671
You mind if I ask you something,
Yukine?

259
00:11:54,255 --> 00:11:56,341
This might be
a little self-serving,

260
00:11:56,925 --> 00:11:59,093
but still,
I need to hear you say it.

261
00:11:59,761 --> 00:12:01,429
Do you truly want
to get stronger?

262
00:12:01,512 --> 00:12:02,430
[gasps]

263
00:12:03,890 --> 00:12:04,933
Can I do that?

264
00:12:07,518 --> 00:12:08,895
I think it's time
for the dungeon crawl

265
00:12:08,978 --> 00:12:09,896
we talked about.

266
00:12:12,523 --> 00:12:13,608
[footsteps]

267
00:12:14,651 --> 00:12:16,277
[YUKINE]
It's called Dayspring Labyrinth,

268
00:12:16,361 --> 00:12:18,863
but it doesn't strike me
as all that labyrinthine.

269
00:12:19,364 --> 00:12:21,950
[KOUSUKE] Oh, trust me,
it's a labyrinth, all right.

270
00:12:22,533 --> 00:12:24,077
But it's more like
your own personal

271
00:12:24,160 --> 00:12:25,995
and internal labyrinth
you have to overcome

272
00:12:26,454 --> 00:12:28,247
Well, that sounds
a little heady.

273
00:12:28,331 --> 00:12:30,375
And it's different for everyone.

274
00:12:30,458 --> 00:12:32,710
It can be easy or excruciating.

275
00:12:33,461 --> 00:12:35,838
You'll be facing
the strongest person imaginable.

276
00:12:37,382 --> 00:12:38,925
It's kind of weird, right?

277
00:12:39,342 --> 00:12:40,718
You enter with a party,

278
00:12:40,802 --> 00:12:43,179
but you all have to go off
and fight on your own.

279
00:12:43,805 --> 00:12:46,015
[YUKINE] So even though
you start off as a group,

280
00:12:46,099 --> 00:12:48,935
everyone splits up to fight
a different monster all alone?

281
00:12:50,645 --> 00:12:53,064
[KOUSUKE] Yep. But if you win,

282
00:12:53,147 --> 00:12:55,108
you're given the option
to join your friends.

283
00:12:55,608 --> 00:12:57,485
Lend them a hand in battle
if they need it.

284
00:12:58,361 --> 00:13:01,572
All right then, this is where
we go our separate ways.

285
00:13:02,198 --> 00:13:03,324
[YUKINE] Okay.

286
00:13:03,658 --> 00:13:05,660
[KOUSUKE] Listen, I want you
to remember something.

287
00:13:05,743 --> 00:13:06,703
[YUKINE] What's that?

288
00:13:06,995 --> 00:13:09,122
The enemy
it'll pit you against in there,

289
00:13:09,205 --> 00:13:11,416
I promise you
that you can defeat them.

290
00:13:11,499 --> 00:13:13,418
I know for a fact
that you can win.

291
00:13:13,501 --> 00:13:15,545
-You think so?
-That's right.

292
00:13:16,087 --> 00:13:18,172
You might start
to lose hope in yourself,

293
00:13:18,256 --> 00:13:19,674
but you can win.

294
00:13:20,258 --> 00:13:21,926
I need you to trust me.

295
00:13:22,010 --> 00:13:23,803
Even if something goes wrong,

296
00:13:23,886 --> 00:13:26,055
I'll look after you
for the rest of my life.

297
00:13:26,639 --> 00:13:29,559
So yeah, you can even lose
on purpose if you want.

298
00:13:30,977 --> 00:13:33,062
Anyway, I'm heading in.

299
00:13:35,565 --> 00:13:36,691
[takes deep breath]

300
00:13:38,484 --> 00:13:40,611
[water rushing]

301
00:13:48,077 --> 00:13:48,953
Who's that?

302
00:13:50,371 --> 00:13:51,289
Is it me?

303
00:13:51,914 --> 00:13:53,999
With a katana? [grunts]

304
00:13:54,834 --> 00:13:56,836
[gasping]

305
00:13:56,919 --> 00:13:58,713
This can't be happening.

306
00:13:59,630 --> 00:14:01,799
Suzune? But you're--

307
00:14:03,718 --> 00:14:04,886
[KOUSUKE]
The big difference between

308
00:14:04,969 --> 00:14:06,846
this dungeon and all the others?

309
00:14:06,929 --> 00:14:09,265
Each member
gets their own special monster.

310
00:14:10,266 --> 00:14:11,517
And they take the form
of the most

311
00:14:11,601 --> 00:14:13,269
intimidating person you know,

312
00:14:13,352 --> 00:14:15,271
or whoever caused
your worst trauma.

313
00:14:16,397 --> 00:14:19,442
Poor Yukine gets both,
all wrapped up in one.

314
00:14:20,068 --> 00:14:22,028
-She'll face her own sister.
-[wind howling]

315
00:14:22,695 --> 00:14:23,780
As for me,

316
00:14:23,863 --> 00:14:25,239
only one person it can be.

317
00:14:26,657 --> 00:14:28,242
And there he is.

318
00:14:28,326 --> 00:14:29,577
Iori!

319
00:14:31,871 --> 00:14:34,207
♪

320
00:14:34,290 --> 00:14:36,417
Ready when you are, Iori!

321
00:14:38,628 --> 00:14:39,587
[Kousuke grunts]

322
00:14:40,380 --> 00:14:42,757
[laughs]
Starting off with magic, huh?

323
00:14:43,424 --> 00:14:44,842
What did you expect?

324
00:14:44,926 --> 00:14:46,552
I mean, he is the manifestation

325
00:14:46,636 --> 00:14:48,429
of the protagonist
at full potential!

326
00:14:49,055 --> 00:14:50,640
Why don't we give this
a shot then?

327
00:14:50,723 --> 00:14:53,059
[grunting]

328
00:14:54,477 --> 00:14:56,312
Not bad! [gasps]

329
00:14:57,438 --> 00:14:59,023
[grunting]

330
00:14:59,732 --> 00:15:02,110
Iori is like an infinite
multiverse of potential.

331
00:15:03,111 --> 00:15:04,195
As a protagonist,

332
00:15:04,529 --> 00:15:06,781
you can max out his stats
in physical combat.

333
00:15:07,365 --> 00:15:10,535
Or you can make him specialize
in casting long-range magic.

334
00:15:11,786 --> 00:15:14,705
He definitely packs a punch.
Although,

335
00:15:14,789 --> 00:15:17,291
he's pathetic
compared to the Iori I know!

336
00:15:18,292 --> 00:15:19,585
Not even close.

337
00:15:19,669 --> 00:15:21,420
Iori would never be this weak.

338
00:15:21,879 --> 00:15:23,089
There's only one other character

339
00:15:23,172 --> 00:15:24,507
who can rival
the amount of spells

340
00:15:24,590 --> 00:15:27,176
and skills at his disposal,
and that's Nanami.

341
00:15:29,011 --> 00:15:32,056
Luckily, he doesn't have
the power of a magic stole!

342
00:15:32,140 --> 00:15:34,350
The protagonist has true power.

343
00:15:34,934 --> 00:15:37,437
And he'll get much stronger
before our face-off.

344
00:15:39,230 --> 00:15:40,731
So come on!

345
00:15:40,815 --> 00:15:43,067
Can I afford to lose
to this thing?

346
00:15:43,151 --> 00:15:45,987
I'll never be worthy
to challenge a genuine opponent,

347
00:15:46,070 --> 00:15:47,822
not if I falter here!

348
00:15:47,905 --> 00:15:50,241
[grunts]
So that's not gonna happen!

349
00:15:51,033 --> 00:15:54,412
[yelling]

350
00:15:54,871 --> 00:15:57,915
Crush him! It's gotta be
a staggering defeat!

351
00:15:57,999 --> 00:15:59,584
He's just a sad copy!

352
00:16:00,042 --> 00:16:01,544
It's not Iori!

353
00:16:01,627 --> 00:16:02,670
The Iori I'm aiming for

354
00:16:02,753 --> 00:16:04,630
is the strongest version
possible!

355
00:16:07,967 --> 00:16:10,636
[yells]

356
00:16:12,013 --> 00:16:13,431
It's slow right now,

357
00:16:13,514 --> 00:16:15,224
but his power's growing!

358
00:16:15,308 --> 00:16:17,310
That's how it works with Iori!

359
00:16:19,645 --> 00:16:22,023
I may be
the stronger one right now,

360
00:16:22,523 --> 00:16:24,442
but that can only last
for so long.

361
00:16:24,901 --> 00:16:27,111
Iori's about to catch up
at an explosive pace.

362
00:16:28,029 --> 00:16:29,530
And I'll be in trouble
if he doesn't.

363
00:16:30,072 --> 00:16:31,032
It needs to happen

364
00:16:31,407 --> 00:16:32,867
to guide the heroines
to a happy ending.

365
00:16:33,576 --> 00:16:35,703
And I need to
keep getting stronger as well!

366
00:16:36,579 --> 00:16:37,705
[shadow Iori gasps]

367
00:16:37,788 --> 00:16:39,165
Sword Drawing Arts!

368
00:16:40,082 --> 00:16:40,999
Flash!

369
00:16:41,083 --> 00:16:42,001
[bangs]

370
00:16:49,509 --> 00:16:51,093
Worthless cosplayer.

371
00:16:51,719 --> 00:16:53,012
Time to join Yukine.

372
00:16:56,891 --> 00:16:58,726
♪

373
00:16:58,809 --> 00:17:00,686
[YUKINE] One of
the first things I remember

374
00:17:01,312 --> 00:17:02,396
was the realization

375
00:17:02,480 --> 00:17:03,981
I could never win
against Suzune.

376
00:17:04,690 --> 00:17:07,860
It didn't matter what it was,
I was always bound to lose.

377
00:17:08,527 --> 00:17:10,988
Everything she did
was impressive to my young eyes.

378
00:17:11,948 --> 00:17:14,325
I chalked it up to the age gap
to avoid jealousy.

379
00:17:15,660 --> 00:17:16,786
But it didn't take long

380
00:17:16,869 --> 00:17:18,913
to realize
how truly gifted she was.

381
00:17:19,872 --> 00:17:21,457
And that's when
I accepted the fact

382
00:17:21,541 --> 00:17:23,751
I could never
possibly surpass her.

383
00:17:24,835 --> 00:17:28,005
And, as most
self-fulfilling prophecies go,

384
00:17:28,089 --> 00:17:31,425
I never came close to winning,
not a single time.

385
00:17:31,509 --> 00:17:33,594
[slashes]

386
00:17:33,678 --> 00:17:37,431
It's her exact swordplay,
but that means...

387
00:17:41,602 --> 00:17:43,563
I feel like
she can see right through me.

388
00:17:47,149 --> 00:17:48,401
What the?

389
00:17:48,693 --> 00:17:51,570
She's moving so fast!
There's no way I can keep up!

390
00:17:51,654 --> 00:17:53,364
-[slashes]
-[Yukine grunts]

391
00:17:53,948 --> 00:17:55,700
[gasps] But that connected!

392
00:17:56,367 --> 00:17:58,828
Stay calm.
You can cut her again.

393
00:17:59,328 --> 00:18:01,414
Yes! You know these attacks.

394
00:18:01,497 --> 00:18:03,582
They're no different
from your sister's!

395
00:18:03,666 --> 00:18:05,710
Redirect and cut!

396
00:18:05,793 --> 00:18:06,961
Again?

397
00:18:07,628 --> 00:18:10,256
Right,
why would this be any different?

398
00:18:10,840 --> 00:18:13,551
No matter how good I am,
she'll always be better.

399
00:18:13,634 --> 00:18:15,720
It's the same
with President Monica,

400
00:18:16,304 --> 00:18:18,431
and the principal
outranks them both.

401
00:18:22,351 --> 00:18:24,395
Shion and Fran stand beside me,

402
00:18:25,146 --> 00:18:28,190
and then Takioto and Ludie
are both hot on my heels.

403
00:18:28,858 --> 00:18:33,029
All of them, they all possess
some exceptional gift or talent.

404
00:18:34,322 --> 00:18:37,366
Why was my sister so convinced
I could be the strongest?

405
00:18:38,034 --> 00:18:39,201
It doesn't make sense.

406
00:18:39,869 --> 00:18:40,786
[sighs]

407
00:18:41,078 --> 00:18:43,164
Has my naginata
always been this heavy?

408
00:18:43,914 --> 00:18:46,584
And has her shadow
always loomed this large?

409
00:18:50,463 --> 00:18:53,382
I guess she must've decided
I'm not even worth fighting.

410
00:18:54,550 --> 00:18:55,718
And she's right.

411
00:18:55,801 --> 00:18:57,678
-I'm not worth anything--
-[KOUSUKE] Yukine!

412
00:19:00,097 --> 00:19:01,182
[YUKINE] Takioto!

413
00:19:02,975 --> 00:19:04,602
I need you to trust me.

414
00:19:04,685 --> 00:19:06,270
Even if something goes wrong,

415
00:19:06,354 --> 00:19:08,522
I'll look after you
for the rest of my life.

416
00:19:09,023 --> 00:19:10,024
So yeah,

417
00:19:10,316 --> 00:19:12,193
you can even lose
on purpose if you want.

418
00:19:12,276 --> 00:19:13,235
♪

419
00:19:13,319 --> 00:19:14,403
[chuckles]

420
00:19:14,695 --> 00:19:16,530
You know, you're starting
to sound like the hero

421
00:19:16,614 --> 00:19:18,824
from some kind of
cheesy romance novel.

422
00:19:19,659 --> 00:19:20,951
What's this feeling?

423
00:19:21,035 --> 00:19:23,871
Why am I suddenly surging
with power?

424
00:19:24,747 --> 00:19:27,500
Listen, sis,
everyone says I'm a genius,

425
00:19:27,583 --> 00:19:29,835
but the truth is,
I'm just a regular person.

426
00:19:30,503 --> 00:19:32,088
The same as you.

427
00:19:32,588 --> 00:19:34,840
[YUKINE] That's right.
She was right.

428
00:19:35,633 --> 00:19:37,677
Genius or not,
she was still human.

429
00:19:38,386 --> 00:19:40,638
And yeah, we're the same.

430
00:19:41,138 --> 00:19:42,181
We're just human.

431
00:19:42,890 --> 00:19:44,058
But that's all I need.

432
00:19:44,475 --> 00:19:46,102
There's no reason I can't win.

433
00:19:46,477 --> 00:19:47,895
It just hasn't happened yet.

434
00:19:48,729 --> 00:19:51,023
If I fail,
Takioto can take me in.

435
00:19:51,107 --> 00:19:53,067
[chuckles] That actually sounds

436
00:19:53,150 --> 00:19:54,568
-kind of fun.
-Huh?

437
00:19:55,194 --> 00:19:56,320
[YUKINE] Hey, Suzune!

438
00:19:57,113 --> 00:19:58,823
I never once stopped training.

439
00:19:58,906 --> 00:20:00,449
Not even after you died!

440
00:20:00,533 --> 00:20:02,493
I'm keeping my promise to you.

441
00:20:02,910 --> 00:20:04,412
I'll show her what I can do.

442
00:20:04,495 --> 00:20:06,414
And I'll show Takioto.

443
00:20:06,497 --> 00:20:08,624
This is the path
I've chosen to walk,

444
00:20:09,083 --> 00:20:10,626
and this is my technique.

445
00:20:11,419 --> 00:20:12,420
Take a look!

446
00:20:12,711 --> 00:20:15,005
This is who I've become!
And what I can do!

447
00:20:15,965 --> 00:20:17,508
[grunts]

448
00:20:19,844 --> 00:20:21,303
She regenerates?

449
00:20:21,804 --> 00:20:23,889
I wish my shadow
had been so tenacious.

450
00:20:23,973 --> 00:20:25,349
[clanging]

451
00:20:30,813 --> 00:20:32,189
It's so beautiful.

452
00:20:34,984 --> 00:20:37,194
[YUKINE] Every type of sword
has this in common.

453
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:40,156
The flash of a blade
carries a "soul."

454
00:20:42,199 --> 00:20:43,868
A dragon!

455
00:20:43,951 --> 00:20:46,203
Her slashes carry
the soul of a dragon!

456
00:20:46,287 --> 00:20:47,204
[YUKINE] Now watch this!

457
00:20:50,875 --> 00:20:51,751
[grunting]

458
00:20:53,043 --> 00:20:54,795
[gasps] There it is!

459
00:20:54,879 --> 00:20:56,797
That's why
I can't help but adore her!

460
00:20:57,423 --> 00:20:59,091
This is the moment
she claims her title

461
00:20:59,175 --> 00:21:00,968
as the Water Dragon Princess!

462
00:21:01,051 --> 00:21:03,220
The reason why fans
ranked her in the Big Three!

463
00:21:03,888 --> 00:21:05,097
Her secret technique.

464
00:21:08,726 --> 00:21:10,311
Nine-Headed Dragon!

465
00:21:12,855 --> 00:21:13,773
[water splashing]

466
00:21:19,236 --> 00:21:20,738
♪

467
00:21:22,114 --> 00:21:23,741
[footsteps]

468
00:21:23,824 --> 00:21:26,619
[YUKINE] I'm sorry,
but I've gotta ask again.

469
00:21:26,702 --> 00:21:29,413
-[KOUSUKE] Ask me what?
-How do you know what you know?

470
00:21:29,497 --> 00:21:30,456
[KOUSUKE] Oh, um...

471
00:21:31,665 --> 00:21:33,417
Sorry. Forget that I asked.

472
00:21:33,501 --> 00:21:36,462
There's nothing
to apologize for. I'd ask too.

473
00:21:37,630 --> 00:21:38,881
Trust me, I get it.

474
00:21:38,964 --> 00:21:40,591
I know it all seems suspicious.

475
00:21:41,008 --> 00:21:44,011
Even just now.
And really? I wanna explain.

476
00:21:44,803 --> 00:21:46,680
But I can't right now.

477
00:21:46,764 --> 00:21:48,641
Do you mind
waiting just a bit longer?

478
00:21:49,058 --> 00:21:50,017
Yeah, of course.

479
00:21:50,684 --> 00:21:53,020
It's clearly a difficult thing
for you to talk about, right?

480
00:21:53,103 --> 00:21:54,772
I've got one condition, though.

481
00:21:55,189 --> 00:21:57,900
If you're ever in trouble,
I want you to come to me.

482
00:21:57,983 --> 00:22:00,444
Doesn't matter what it is,
you've got my support.

483
00:22:00,903 --> 00:22:01,904
Thanks a lot.

484
00:22:03,030 --> 00:22:04,907
[YUKINE] Now,
let's get back to training.

485
00:22:04,990 --> 00:22:06,158
[KOUSUKE] Yeah!

486
00:22:10,037 --> 00:22:11,997
[♪ closing theme song playing]

